        <span class="tag">what's in the box</span>
        <h2 class="section-h2">Deal discovery to drafted pitch, one loop.</h2>
        <p class="what-desc">Not a scraped lead list. The studio finds the companies worth your time, proves who they are, and writes what you'd actually send them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="what-grid reveal d1">
        <div class="wc"><div class="wc-n">01</div><h3>Deal discovery</h3><p>Type a company — or press "find more" on an empty box. The studio suggests lookalikes worth pitching and scores each one against what you told it to hunt.</p></div>
        <div class="wc"><div class="wc-n">02</div><h3>Research that shows its work</h3><p>It reads the target's own website before anything else runs. Every pitch lists the pages it opened and the same-named companies it ruled out.</p></div>
        <div class="wc"><div class="wc-n">03</div><h3>The pitch, drafted</h3><p>Pitch deck, one-pager, cold-email sequence and written proposal — on your brand, in your voice, every block editable in place.</p></div>
        <div class="wc"><div class="wc-n">04</div><h3>People, sourced honestly</h3><p>Decision-makers are named only when a credible source backs the name — rated confirmed, likely or unverified. No source, no name.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

